      "writtenOn": "2019-05-21T15:12:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This can read beyond the end of the slice. I think this is safe because the address of the load is always rounded down to the nearest 16 byte boundary and the address points at most 15 bytes beyond the end of the slice, meaning we can\u0027t cross a page boundary. It would be good to have a comment to that effect somewhere here.",
